## Show inherited outgoing relations on subclasses

Context: OWL already treats subclass instances as valid subjects of a parent
object-property, but Studio, the entity panel, and Mapping only showed
relations whose declared domain was the class itself. Subclasses now surface
those outgoing relations at read time without duplicating OWL or mapping SQL.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/OntologyClassModel.py
   Add ancestor walk and `outgoing_relations_for_class`.
2. tests/units/ontology/test_inherited_relations.py
   Cover own vs inherited, multi-level, cycles, missing parent, no mutation.
3. src/front/static/global/js/ontology-inheritance.js
   Mirror the helper for Ontology and Mapping pages.
4. src/front/templates/ontology.html / src/front/templates/mapping.html
   Load the JS helper before the map scripts.
5. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   Draw dashed inherited subclass-to-range edges and a legend item.
6. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-map.css
   Style `.map-link.inherited`.
7. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   Read-only inherited-relations list on the entity Details tab.
8. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   Inherited edges plus Status-tab links that open the declaring mapping.
9. src/front/static/mapping/css/mapping-design.css
   Style `.mapping-map-link.inherited`.
10. tests/units/front/test_inherited_relations_ui.py
    Source contracts for helper load order, graphs, and panels.
11. docs/user-guide.md / docs/features.md / docs/architecture.md
    Document dashed inherited edges and mapping reuse.

